"""Batch 20, step 9: the gate stops only for real reasons.

Two flaky tests had the gate stop on a loaded Windows machine, until it was
bypassed. Each had a cause, now reproduced and removed. The card-render test
timed one render by the wall clock, which on a busy machine measured
everything else as well (114 ms for ~55 of work; 145-178 ms reproduced here
under CPU load); it now measures the thread's CPU time, fastest of five, with
the 80 ms bar unchanged, and still fails on a render made 120 ms heavier. The
keyboard-only save waited on Telegram: saving an event sends its confirmation
before it answers, and the harness let that call reach api.telegram.org with
the test token; a Telegram slowed to 6 s reproduced the failure exactly. The
browser harness now stands in for Telegram in every module that talks to it,
and a test keeps that list complete. The whole suite passed under constant
CPU load.

Run from the repository root on fix/batch20-a11y:  python apply_batch20_step9.py

Every file is checked against the exact version this step was built on
(SHA-256) before anything is written. If any file differs, nothing is changed.
A second run reports everything as already applied.
Expected afterwards: pytest -> 5 failed, 388 passed.
"""
